    {
      "id": "841c950a-e79a-4516-83a4-daa4882b4b58",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        480,
        -800
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Lost Deal Reason AI analysis | Save to GHL back\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow receives a webhook for a lost deal, retrieves the related GoHighLevel contact and opportunity, and verifies that both are valid and the opportunity is actually marked lost. It then fetches the contact’s conversations, processes and filters the message history, and only continues when there is suitable conversation content to analyze. A Gemini-powered AI Agent extracts a structured lost-deal reason and posts that reason back to GoHighLevel as a note.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Webhook node URL as the trigger endpoint in GoHighLevel for lost opportunity/deal events.\n- Connect the HighLevel nodes with valid GoHighLevel credentials and confirm the contact and opportunity IDs are mapped from the webhook payload.\n- Configure the LeadConnector/GHL HTTP Request nodes with the correct API token, location/account details, API version headers, and conversation/note endpoint parameters.\n- Set up Google Gemini credentials for the AI Agent’s chat model and confirm the Structured Output Parser schema matches the fields expected in the final note.\n- Review the IF conditions and Code nodes to ensure they match your exact contact, opportunity status, and conversation filtering rules.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the conversation filtering code, the minimum-message IF condition, the AI prompt/schema, and the final note format to match your sales process or CRM reporting needs."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
